        "id": "419zwuSNyFff"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This time, we ask the floorplanner to respect the die size supplied with the option ``FP_SIZING`` as **absolute**. Run the floorplanning again."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fE2JMbIGyL5c"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "Floorplan = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.Floorplan\")\n",
        "floorplan = Floorplan(FP_SIZING=\"absolute\", state_in=synthesis.state_out)\n",
        "floorplan.start()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7a3y0OI-lRQt"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Inspect the output on die area and confirm that the new dimension is in place.\n",
        "\n",
        "What is the core area in μm${}^2$?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n",
        "\n",
        "Next, we will try again with the I/O placement."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "AE11HZyEyd8j"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "TapEndcapInsertion = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.TapEndcapInsertion\")\n",
        "tdi = TapEndcapInsertion(state_in=floorplan.state_out)\n",
        "tdi.start()\n",
        "\n",
        "IOPlacement = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.IOPlacement\")\n",
        "ioplace = IOPlacement(state_in=tdi.state_out)\n",
        "ioplace.start()\n",
        "display(ioplace)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2c5ZaeQrmLDj"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "If it is **not successful**, return to the first box in **Step 3** and enter a bigger width and height.\n",
        "\n",
        "Which metal layer(s) is/are used for the I/O pins?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n",
        "\n",
        "Estimate the pitch of the I/O pins. The pitch is the distance between two pins.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "iKayBNRMZeBs"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We will proceed with the remaining steps of the physical implementation."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Cgco78c20COs"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# generate power distribution network (PDN)\n",
        "GeneratePDN = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.GeneratePDN\")\n",
        "pdn = GeneratePDN(\n",
        "    state_in=ioplace.state_out,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_AUTO_ADJUST=True,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_VPITCH=25,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_HPITCH=25,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_VOFFSET=5,\n",
        "    FP_PDN_HOFFSET=5,\n",
        ")\n",
        "pdn.start()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Global placement\n",
        "GlobalPlacement = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.GlobalPlacement\")\n",
        "gpl = GlobalPlacement(state_in=pdn.state_out)\n",
        "gpl.start()\n",
        "\n",
        "# run detailed placement\n",
        "DetailedPlacement = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.DetailedPlacement\")\n",
        "dpl = DetailedPlacement(state_in=gpl.state_out)\n",
        "dpl.start()\n",
        "\n",
        "display(dpl)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "TZGCiRqjZeBs"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Next, we will route the design."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "rMzEX4di0a2S"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Global routing\n",
        "GlobalRouting = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.GlobalRouting\")\n",
        "grt = GlobalRouting(state_in=dpl.state_out)\n",
        "grt.start()\n",
        "\n",
        "DetailedRouting = Step.factory.get(\"OpenROAD.DetailedRouting\")\n",
        "drt = DetailedRouting(state_in=grt.state_out)\n",
        "drt.start()\n",
        "display(drt)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "QDT2NcQBZeBt"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Inspect the log and the routed design. What is the final total wirelength?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n",
        "\n",
        "You may consider this as the length required to connect the logic circuit with the I/O pins.\n",
        "\n",
        "Please save a copy of the picture of this final layout for your final assignment."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "aE1_dsAnZeBt"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Step 4: Challenges of inserting I/O pads"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Qh_PZIhc1xiH"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "From the task above, we have successfully assigned I/O pins around the die, but without any I/O pads. I/O pads are necessary to provide electrical protection and an area for wire bonding.\n",
        "\n",
        "A typical in-line pad pitch required for 0.18 μm technology is [70 μm](https://www.onsemi.com/PowerSolutions/content.do?id=16679). What would be the dimension of the die if in-line pads are added?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n",
        "\n",
        "How many percentage of the area is used as the core in this case?\n",
        "\n",
        "*Enter your answer here*\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "B1dnpyQk1xiO"
      }
